<figure id="S2.T2" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 2: </span>Results on IEMOCAP (4-way) and CMU-MOSEI dataset compared with previous works. For sentiment classification on the CMU-MOSEI dataset, we trained an independent binary classifier for each emotion. The <span id="S2.T2.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">bolded</span> results indicate the best performance, while the <span id="S2.T2.6" class="ltx_text ltx_underline">underlined</span> results represent the second best performance. <sup id="S2.T2.7" class="ltx_sup">∗</sup> denotes identical scores for Fear (84.47) and Surprise (85.66) due to the baselines’ binary classifiers failing to separate the positive and negative classes. </figcaption>
